    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0578" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.857 An 2/95</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 30, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose a copy of a
                    telegram which has just been received from Vienna under date of the 29th.<anchor
                        n="85" xml:id="d474-f1"/> I assume that by tomorrow or next day we will
                    receive the full text of the note.</p>
                <p>From the summary given by Mr. Penfield it would seem as if the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ancona</hi> case offered possibilities of solution.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d474-f1" n="85" xml:id="d474-f1-content">
